#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096428 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "87747005-ce77-5ec6-9f44-af074633aa98" :question/math-academy-id "e-401" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=4-x^2$ between $x=-1,$ $x=2,$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown below. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?\n\n![](images/b5/b517da6e730ac50341b133a60ae8ab99cfed7b2ce92638e6028bb3fac6fbf9da.png)" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} f(x_k)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_k = a + k\\Delta x$ with $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{2-(-1)}{3} = \\dfrac 3 3 = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(-1+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-(k-1)^{2}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(4-{k}^{2}+2k-1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}(3+2k-{k}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096429 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "af666c8f-dfb7-548e-a8f1-1922d4c2fdc5" :question/math-academy-id "e-402" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{ x}{2}\\right)$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $3$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^n f(x_i)\\Delta x,\n$$\n\nwhere $x_i = a + i\\Delta x$ and $\\Delta x = \\dfrac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nNote that here we are using the index $i$ instead of $k.$ It doesn't matter which letter we use for the counter.\n\nWe're told that there are $n=3$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\Delta x = \\dfrac{3-0}{3} = \\dfrac{3}{3} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{i}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536816 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12436895-69cb-503c-8085-217ca08ec281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{i}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536313} {:answer/id #uuid "43b8f5fb-30a4-58cc-b827-a3c6c0f1627e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2i}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536386} {:answer/id #uuid "4eec80dc-bf63-5e26-a70a-c9df0a844d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536417} {:answer/id #uuid "af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536568} {:answer/id #uuid "d6cf2865-18ea-59ba-9dab-3d90e49f0104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af0d5166-e6c8-504d-975f-ece6f9efdfce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536568} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ee4b5b3-c121-55ee-96bd-54041a866832" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "21c1c6c9-f8f1-50f1-a9ef-3d13b0e5c684" :question/math-academy-id "q-116626" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+2}$ between $x=-2$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $7$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=7$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-2$ and $b=2.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-2)}{7}=\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+i\\cdot \\frac{4}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}f(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})\\cdot \\frac{4}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{(-2+\\frac{4i}{7})+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{4i}{7}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536901 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6j}{n}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f0daa64-ab0d-5c7d-bc74-4d0c2bf2920a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6j}{n}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536418} :answer-field/id #uuid "da4b8589-0630-5be5-bada-40a46902ce0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536792}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fe245032-d155-5a02-8475-f1836177bbab" :question/math-academy-id "q-315710" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+1)$ between $x=-1$ and $x=2$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $j$ and $n.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=2.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-1+\\frac{3j}{n})+1)] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6j}{n}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{k+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0e29592-9ea2-5a39-a74f-62ec0996efbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{k+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536569} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cfdfcb5-7c50-5afa-92b2-1f208f863466" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536705}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62141b5-a243-5a9b-bfab-d11b88f8be6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-345028" :question/problem "![](images/7d/7d7a51344b945f502ace0aa7b9d5dee46514a465adda7666d83fe91bd2ffb3a2.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$ between $x=0$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $k.$*\n\n${S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum ${S}_{L}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{L}={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{4-1}f(0+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}f(k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{1+k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf9c4b37-e372-57d7-a0be-33097ed1ca8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536611} :answer-field/id #uuid "07fff1fe-7a31-59f7-8640-95363928e02e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536703}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2bcca121-9116-5327-93c6-12a3a1649264" :question/math-academy-id "q-345038" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=(x+1)^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is   \n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n=4$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=3.$ So, the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-(-1)}{4}=\\frac{4}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(-1+i)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{(-1+i+1)}^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\,{i}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186318961 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b905cd6e-ce52-52c8-9a4a-b6ea3feabbf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b905cd6e-ce52-52c8-9a4a-b6ea3feabbf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318183} :answer-field/id #uuid "97d92250-02b3-5131-88bc-cb707adc8d67" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318760}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1af811e2-d217-57d3-a9b2-d6a86ea6f17b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345052" :question/problem "![](images/f3/f321b063e3bc76eeb5b426d00cbf94451a06cec928008eaadc965547691c412a.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=4+x$ between $x=0,$ $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a right Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ in sigma notation?\n\n*Hint: Write down the expression in terms of $i.$*\n\n${S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}($\n{{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=4$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-0}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum ${S}_{R}$ can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{R}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(0+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}f(i) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}(4+i).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a457ee-275f-5ec7-a5b0-1ffb26f9cc22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536577} {:answer/id #uuid "c4de2e59-74dc-5cf4-9fcb-a0a43b5dac86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536596} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f9bf07-ae92-50c1-ab4e-b76d5bf6aefd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=1}^{3}\\sqrt{i+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536598} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5ee95f-0280-530e-bb69-7f936cd23797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536606} {:answer/id #uuid "fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb121efb-f9e3-53b8-983a-b475b7803a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536686} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8832846-ab8f-51d9-b35e-38e81a04d8b6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a82c733-fd67-5ad0-94b7-aa145f6ffd91" :question/math-academy-id "q-49264" :question/problem "![](images/35/35b881e8bb04eb192967ebc94945850fb0450012675369facd4efb41c611aaab.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}$ between $x=1$, $x=4$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{i}=a+iΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=1$ and $b=4,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{4-1}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{i})Δx & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{n-1}f(a+iΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{3-1}f(1+i\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}f(i+1) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=0}^{2}\\sqrt{i+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096629 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d01d6ed-1c25-5170-a1ad-7a4fa0103db7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Right Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16912225-3f70-5541-b574-3061e2e7b38e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{3n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536320} {:answer/id #uuid "242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536336} {:answer/id #uuid "761dcd9a-706c-5db6-a6b8-883ea8047a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n-1}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536482} {:answer/id #uuid "9b62e5a4-9e97-5400-851f-d6ea027be307" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{2}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2j}{n})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536534} {:answer/id #uuid "e1d1bf4f-0539-5436-aeaf-4b61a267639b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{j}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "242d5a8d-320a-55dd-af45-50bb63662fa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536336} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a1a980a-9817-5cc2-b963-bee9f053f5b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3994f797-7a6e-5428-aacb-fe36a9051f76" :question/math-academy-id "q-49364" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a right Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The right Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're told that there are $n$ subintervals. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{n}=\\frac{3}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the right Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{3}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[f(\\frac{3j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{3}{n}] \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}[\\frac{3}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3j}{n})].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ab988cf-5693-58a8-b278-e05c02100c50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(4-\\frac{4j}{n}+\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{n})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536323} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf153cd-dbf3-5f7a-9e7a-e147bed59a38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{1}\\frac{2}{n}(5-\\frac{4j}{n}+\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536353} {:answer/id #uuid "36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536370} {:answer/id #uuid "83db7859-91ab-56dc-83ce-dbb89d1f2482" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(5-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536500} {:answer/id #uuid "f7fd2c5c-cf9d-5138-8ac5-87eba6bf55c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\frac{2}{n}(\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b76477-1bee-5cfd-af35-4972e78ad218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536370} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c4f8a5-a724-5fb9-9af0-afee36d1582d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9fc617a-f5be-5a74-8545-9128626b78b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49383" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=5-{x}^{2}$ between $x=-1$ and $x=1$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $n$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of subintervals, ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$, and $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nThe endpoints indicate that $a=-1$ and $b=1,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-(-1)}{n}=\\frac{2}{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+j\\cdot \\frac{2}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})\\cdot \\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}[5-{(-1+\\frac{2j}{n})}^{2}]\\frac{2}{n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}\\frac{2}{n}(4+\\frac{4j}{n}-\\frac{4{j}^{2}}{{n}^{2}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c148ce-3d4b-5f82-be22-94b1b7a941d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{8}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536358} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc7096b-e4d0-5551-8b4c-698c994185de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536410} {:answer/id #uuid "5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536429} {:answer/id #uuid "79aff7b5-6b64-51d5-8c15-e972a08c75b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536487} {:answer/id #uuid "d48e153e-cc47-599d-abb7-f430aae869da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5479d04f-11d8-52ff-a10f-c5daf44d5b8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536429} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9b02b04-3990-5647-8a7e-f4a0b6db0f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536802}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a6becce-61cc-5b53-a5ff-f772c9293a84" :question/math-academy-id "q-73069" :question/problem "The area under the curve $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ between $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and the $x$-axis is approximated by a left Riemann sum using $4$ subintervals of equal length. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{j}=a+jΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nWe're given that $n=4$ subintervals.  The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{(\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)}{4}=\\frac{\\pi }{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{j})Δx & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{n-1}f(a+jΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{4-1}f(0+j\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}f(\\frac{j\\pi }{8})\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}{\\sum }_{j=0}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{j\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536847 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62c34646-f7cf-5ffd-b957-4151bdbb5e44" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Left Riemann Sum in Sigma Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06c395f8-cf42-52aa-a803-43591ce1552c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{k}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536295} {:answer/id #uuid "57c77a3f-a887-515d-9a85-dfc4702748fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{8-{k}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536438} {:answer/id #uuid "9d636130-3c2c-52dd-9e9b-3376ca8624c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{8-{k}^{2}-2k}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536538} {:answer/id #uuid "e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{9-{k}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536638} {:answer/id #uuid "fab745cb-883b-50ae-b463-3c48ccdfe0a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{3}\\sqrt{6-{k}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2bc2c15-5ae4-5cc7-8401-515b22401c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{9-{k}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536638} :answer-field/id #uuid "61f4da89-3768-5682-9582-88618e04b971" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186536743}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83ed0f7d-e76a-53b6-8cf6-264c24acad16" :question/math-academy-id "q-73139" :question/problem "![](images/17/17f6b2ab535408802ef2776eea2db41ac20b17f3568e245ee87b13f05767203f.png)\n\nThe area under the curve $y=\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}$ between $x=0$, $x=3$ and the $x$-axis is approximated using a left Riemann sum, as shown above. What is the expression for the Riemann sum in sigma notation?" :question/worked-solution "The left Riemann sum for $y=f(x)$ with a regular step size in sigma notation is\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{k}=a+kΔx$ with $Δx=\\frac{b-a}{n}.$ \n\nFrom the diagram, we see that there are $n=3$ rectangles. The endpoints indicate that $a=0$ and $b=3,$ so the step size is\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-0}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using sigma notation, the left Riemann sum can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f({x}_{k})Δx & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{n-1}f(a+kΔx)Δx \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{3-1}f(0+k\\cdot 1)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}f(k) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{k=0}^{2}\\sqrt{9-{k}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
